      "published_at": "2026-11-09T21:03:39+00:00",
      "summary": "🥟 Run tests with Bun The test runner now runs under Bun . Bun transpiles your TypeScript test files itself, so Playwright does not use Babel or its compilation cache. Pass the --bun flag, because without it bunx playwright test runs on Node.js: bunx --bun playwright test Our CI runs the test runner tests under Bun 1.4.3 on Linux. Some features work differently under Bun: There is no watch mode. UI mode does not run tests again when files change, and --only-changed does not follow imports. Bun loads modules itself, so --tsconfig and the JSX options in tsconfig.json have no effect, and custom ESM loaders are not supported. Stack traces do not include async frames, and API names do not include the class name: click instead of locator.click . This changes some step locations, step titles and error messages. Console output of a test does not get into the trace and UI mode. 🚨 Reports with only",
